A photoresistor which detects light intensity and shows values from range 0 to 1023. When light is above a threshhold intensity , stepper motor rotates. The rotation of 
stepper motor can be considered as curtain actuation.

components used - photoresistor(ldr) , stepper motor , resistor , breadboard , arduino(microcontroller), ULN2003 (stepper motor driver), breadboard power supply.

working of photoresistor - it is a resistor whose value changes when light falls on it. electrons in valence band get energized when light of centain frequency falls on it. Hence, it
is free from bound of nucleus and now can conduct electricity. thus resistance drops when light intensity increases.

working of stepper motor - It works on principle of electromagnetic induction. It is used for precision in angles . The rotation of stepper motors is by taking steps . the stepper
motor used in this project takes 2048 steps to complete 1 revolution. It is driven by the stepper driver. the rotor of stepper has 50 teeth and stator has 48 teeth. A 2 phase 
current is passed through the coils and the motors starts to step.

It is coded in such a way that when ldr reads a value above a certain theshhold , the curtain opens ( motor rotates ) and below a certain value it closes.
the rotation of motor represents curtain actuation.
